# Citation metadata for this book.
#
# GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository" button on the
# repository page. Zenodo also reads it when a release is archived, and its
# values override whatever the GitHub release integration would otherwise
# guess, which is what stops a new release from being filed as software again.
#
# The DOI below is the CONCEPT DOI. It is minted once and always resolves to
# the newest version, so it never has to change here. Each individual version
# also gets its own DOI; those are not recorded in this file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "How to Govern AI: Foundations and Practical Guide to AI Governance"
abstract: >-
  A practitioner's guide to governing artificial intelligence across its full
  lifecycle: scoping and inventory, risk classification, data governance, model
  selection and development, testing and red-teaming, deployment, monitoring,
  incident response, and the governance of generative and agentic systems. It
  reads the EU AI Act, the NIST AI Risk Management Framework, ISO/IEC 42001 and
  sector regulation against each other, and turns them into the artifacts and
  decisions an organization actually has to produce.
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: Ogunseye
    given-names: Shawn
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5774-4965"
version: "2.0"
date-released: 2026-08-01
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.18407349
url: "https://aigov.ogunseye.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShawnOgunseye/GovAI"
# No open licence. The book is all rights reserved; CITATION.cff has no
# free-text rights field, so the statement lives in the README and on the site.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - artificial intelligence
  - EU AI Act
  - NIST AI Risk Management Framework
  - ISO/IEC 42001
  - responsible AI
  - risk management
references:
  - type: book
    title: "Governing AI: Leading Responsible Innovation"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ogunseye
        given-names: Shawn
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5774-4965"
    version: "1.5.2"
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.18407350
    notes: "The first edition, superseded by this one."
